# Small talk and trade questions: does Mara answer like a person who has kept this stall for years?
# speaker | what the customer does (their goal, in their own words) | what Mara faces
elf | You are at Mara's fruit stall in the town market with the warrior. Greet her and ask how long she has kept this stall. | A customer greets her and asks how long she has kept the stall.
elf | Ask which of her fruit is best this week, and why. | The customer asks which fruit is best this week.
warrior | Pick up a pear and ask, bluntly, how you tell if it is ripe. | The warrior asks how to tell a ripe pear.
elf | Ask whether she grows the fruit herself or buys it in. | The customer asks whether she grows the fruit herself.
elf | Ask what market days are like when it rains. | The customer asks what market days are like in the rain.
warrior | Ask which keeps longer on a march, apples or plums. | The warrior asks which keeps longer on a march, apples or plums.
elf | Ask her what she would pack for two travellers on a week's road. | The customer asks what she would pack for two travellers for a week.
warrior | Say that sounds right and ask what it all comes to. | The warrior asks the total for what she suggested.
elf | Thank her and say you will tell other travellers about her stall. | The customer thanks her and promises to send other travellers.
